# Project keep rules for the release build (R8 full mode).
#
# Retrofit, OkHttp, kotlinx.serialization, Hilt/Dagger, Navigation, Coil and the YouTube player ship their own
# consumer rules, and AGP adds the default Android rules. This file only covers what is specific to Cinevo.

# Readable release stack traces: keep line numbers and map them back with build/outputs/mapping/release/mapping.txt.
-keepattributes SourceFile,LineNumberTable
-renamesourcefileattribute SourceFile

# Retrofit hands the generic return type of each TmdbApi method, such as PagedResponseDto<MovieDto>, to the
# kotlinx.serialization converter, which looks the serializer up reflectively through the class's Companion.
# Keep the generic signatures that lookup reads, and keep every DTO (it may still be renamed) so that a type
# reachable only through a TmdbApi signature is never removed.
-keepattributes Signature,InnerClasses,EnclosingMethod
-keep,allowobfuscation @kotlinx.serialization.Serializable class com.app.cinevo.data.remote.dto.**

# The service interface is only created reflectively by Retrofit.create(). Keep its methods and their
# annotations; the names can still be shortened.
-keep,allowobfuscation interface com.app.cinevo.data.remote.TmdbApi { *; }
